# Allowlist, not a denylist: everything is ignored unless re-included below.
#
# This directory is ~500 MB, almost all of it generated state -- session transcripts under
# projects/, file-history/, telemetry/ -- plus a live OAuth credential at .credentials.json.
# The config actually worth versioning is ~286 KB. Ignoring by default means `git add -A`
# cannot stage a credential or a transcript even by mistake; a denylist would leak the first
# time a new state directory appeared upstream.
#
# For a path to be considered at all, every parent directory must also be re-included --
# that is why the directory entries below are paired with their /** globs. Nothing inside
# projects/, cache/, sessions/, plans/ etc. is ever examined, because those directories are
# never re-included and git does not descend into them.

*

!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!CLAUDE.md
!context.md
!settings.json
!hooks/
!hooks/**
!skills/
!skills/**
!scripts/
!scripts/**

# Keep .bak files that sit inside the allowed trees. They are superseded and slated for
# deletion, but committing them once preserves their content in history -- which is the whole
# reason the .bak convention is being retired.
!*.bak

# Re-exclude noise inside the allowed trees. Later patterns win.
skills/**/__pycache__/

# A skill's bootstrapped dependency tree, and any PDF it builds while being tested.
# Both are per-machine and large. Without these, `!skills/**` above re-includes them and
# the untracked files left by a first run make `scripts/sync-config.sh push` refuse to run.
skills/**/_deps*/
skills/**/*.pdf

# Never track a skill's calibration memory. These accumulate direct references to the user's work --
# private repo names, source filenames, internal symbols and defect details -- which is exactly
# what this repo must not carry. The skills recreate these files on demand.
skills/*/memory/
